# The games on this host, one path per arena. Imported into the site block in
# ../Caddyfile on a host whose role is `arena` or `all`.
#
# A path rather than a name per arena, which is the rate-limit lesson the file
# above was rewritten around: adding an arena here costs nothing, and adding a
# name costs one of five certificates a week.
#
# One per zone process. An arena holds every room its zone allows, so the count
# tracks zones rather than seats. The deployment check keeps these routes
# paired with the arena services and the catalog's declared zones.
#
# This is the WebSocket door. The WebTransport one is not here and cannot be:
# a QUIC session is the HTTP/3 connection itself, so the arena terminates it on
# its own UDP port and reads its certificate straight out of the store Caddy
# writes.

handle /metrics/a1* {
	rewrite * /metrics
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:9101
}
handle /metrics/bots* {
	rewrite * /metrics
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:9105
}

handle_path /a1* {
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:9001
}
